    <description>

The Venera 8 Energetic Particles experiment was a Soviet suite of particle
detectors that monitored the flux of charged particles of medium energies in
interplanetary space during cruise and Venus approach, specifically
measuring protons (&gt;30 and 5-10 MeV) and electrons (&gt;.05 MeV) from the
sunward direction; and protons (1-5 and &gt;0.3 MeV) and electrons (&gt;.05 MeV)
from the anti-sunward direction.

        </description>
